      <a href="#spend-less">How to Spend Less</a>
      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Body -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Aldi's Elevation by Millville whey costs about $20 a tub, and in the 2 lb size that works out at roughly $0.80 to $0.95 per 25 g of protein, one of the lowest figures for any flavored whey sold in a US store. The newer 24 oz tub sells at almost the same price, which pushes it to roughly $1.10 to $1.20 per 25 g, about where name brands land on sale. This guide shows the arithmetic, compares it with eggs, chicken, milk, yogurt and tuna, and explains when Elevation stops being the cheap option.
        </p>

        <div id="shelf-price" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What Aldi Protein Powder Costs on the Shelf
          </h2>

          <p>
            Aldi sells one protein powder in its core range: Elevation by Millville whey protein blend, in chocolate and vanilla. For years it came in a 2 lb (32 oz) tub, and coverage from 2024 and 2025 puts the shelf price of that tub at roughly $20. When we checked aldi.us in early November 2026, the newest listings described a 24 oz tub at $19.79, while an older 32 oz vanilla listing was still visible but out of stock.
          </p>

          <p>
            That is the whole story of Aldi protein powder pricing in one sentence: the price has barely moved, but the amount of powder in the tub may have. A shopper who remembers paying $20 for a 2 lb tub and sees a $19.79 tag today could easily assume nothing has changed. If the tub on the shelf is the 24 oz version, they are getting about a quarter less powder for the same money.
          </p>

          <p>
            We cannot confirm whether every store has moved to the smaller tub. Aldi's own help pages say protein powder availability varies by location, and stores often sell through older stock before new packaging arrives. The practical rule is simple. Before you decide whether Elevation is cheap, read the net weight and the servings per container printed on the tub you are holding, not the size you remember.
          </p>

          <p>
            Aldi also rarely discounts Elevation. Unlike name brands, which cycle through coupons, Subscribe and Save offers and big-box sales, Elevation tends to sit at the same shelf price week after week. That makes it predictable rather than spectacular. You will not catch it at half price, but you also will not pay a premium for buying it on the wrong week, which is a real advantage for anyone who buys a tub every few weeks.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
            <p class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-[#38BDF8] mb-4">Elevation at a Glance</p>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-center">
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">~$20</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">2 lb tub, as reported</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">$19.79</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">24 oz tub, aldi.us</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-white">30 g</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Protein per serving (label)</p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-3xl font-black text-[#38BDF8]">$0.80+</p>
                <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs mt-1">Low end per 25 g protein</p>
