          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Aldi protein powder costs about $20 a tub, and whether that is a bargain depends almost entirely on the tub size. In the 2 lb tub, Elevation works out at roughly $0.80 to $0.93 per 25 g of protein, level with milk and bulk chicken and cheaper than almost any flavored whey on a supermarket shelf. In the 24 oz tub at $19.79, it is roughly $1.10 to $1.18, which is fair value but no longer the clear winner.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            So read the net weight before you buy, use the shelf price rather than the app or a reseller, and buy the 2 lb tub whenever you see it. If your store only has the smaller tub, or you need certification, dairy-free protein or a different sweetener, compare against the name brands on cost per 25 g and buy the one you will actually finish.
